/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::disableAnimationPhysics(number recoveryTime, int direction)
\brief Recover animation control before removing the physical rig.

Uses the same collision-aware recovery as setAnimationPhysicsMode(), defaulting
to 0.5 seconds. The rig and its colliders remain active until recovery actually
completes; isAnimationPhysicsEnabled() remains true meanwhile. Blocked or
force-limited recovery may take longer than the requested duration. A new mode
command cancels pending disable. Zero removes the rig immediately.

On completion, restores the Sprite body's saved mode and collision filter and
transfers the selected root body's linear/angular velocity. The explicit or generated rig's
current total mass transfers to the single Sprite body, keeping that body's
previous single-body inertia. This is not a momentum-conserving merge. Mapped
colliders and joints detach; retained mapped Parts remain body-free, and retained body
handles stop contributing mass. Emits action_AnimationPhysicsRecoveryComplete
with disabled true after teardown. Calling without an active rig is harmless.

\param recoveryTime Finite nonnegative seconds; default 0.5, zero for immediate teardown.
\param direction Rotation route; default rotationDirection_AsSpecified.
\note Call outside animation modifiers and locked physics callbacks. Release any manual or Part IK drives explicitly before disabling.
\see setAnimationPhysicsMode(), isAnimationPhysicsEnabled()
\return No value.
*/
